-- Trace data foundation v2.28.0: employer criterion rules pm-eligibility-v3 (Phase 4 closure).
-- GENERATED by scripts/build_transition_content.py from the reviewed JSON. Do not edit by hand.
-- Phase 4 closure (2026-11-17): J12 'currently a product manager' and a current Associate PM; J3 engineering experience before product.
-- Structure preserves AND (all) / OR (any), ranges and required versus preferred. Leaves: years_in_families (reviewed roles in the named role families, from partial dates: 'meets' only when the certain minimum reaches the stated minimum, 'does not meet' only when the possible maximum cannot), product_exposure (confirmed, categorised responsibility evidence in a role of the named families showing a product-ownership area; a job title alone never counts), current_role_in_families and not_transitioning_from (the user's CURRENT confirmed role only; earlier roles never trigger an exclusion), total_years, qualification (an 'or equivalent' clause never gives 'does not meet'; a missing qualification record is unclear, never absence), and stated_condition (a condition the profile cannot show, such as a product domain; always unclear). Preferred criteria are reported but never decide the outcome. Revision v2 (D36): product management tenure leaves list Product Owner and founder families as possible equivalents, which give Unclear (never meets or does not meet on their own); qualifications match the stated field on normalised whole values through explicit aliases, or a degree type (B.E./B.Tech); internships, part-time work and apprenticeships with an unspecified work pattern never count towards the certain minimum. Revision v3: a current-role leaf may list unconfirmed_roles (a role inside the named families that the employer has not said it treats as equivalent; it gives unclear, never meets or does not meet); a years leaf may list before_families (only experience before the first confirmed role in those families counts).
-- Curated public reference content: no user data, no synthetic test data.

-- The two new leaf keys name existing taxonomy entries (checked here; the rule structure is checked by the table's trigger).
do $$
begin
  if exists (select 1 from unnest(array['PM-APM']::text[]) x
              where not exists (select 1 from public.trace_role_taxonomy t where t.role_id = x)) then
    raise exception 'unknown role in unconfirmed_roles';
  end if;
  if exists (select 1 from unnest(array['product_management']::text[]) x
              where not exists (select 1 from public.trace_role_families f where f.role_family = x)) then
    raise exception 'unknown family in before_families';
  end if;
end
$$;

